// #2796: an owning mutable slot assigned a wrapper whose leaf is a PROJECTION
// rooted at a binder that is itself a BORROW.
//
// `spine_leaf_unowned` answers a wrapper's leaf in two arms, and #2793 corrected
// only the `ECall` one. The `EDot` arm went on testing whether the projection's
// root was a spine binder -- which is not evidence that the binder's own `ELet`
// lowering already retained the escaping element, only that it could have. `h`
// here is bound to `Array::get(hs, 0)`, a borrow, so `classify_let_value_heap`
// leaves it at `rc_kind == 0`: no entry in `heap_binding_names`, no scope-end
// drop, so nothing promoted and nothing to duplicate. Declining cost the slot a
// reference `hs` still owns, and its drop released it.
//
// Measured on a stage2 built from `main` at b4697f7, and identically on the
// committed seed: `850` on the RC lane against the bump lane's `770` -- the
// second read of the element answering with the filler, 15, instead of 7.
//
// THIS SHAPE LIVES ALONE, deliberately, and the reason is worth the file.
// It was first written into `rc_wrapper_assign_borrow_test.vibe` next to its
// `ECall` sibling, where it FAILED IDENTICALLY on the fixed and the unfixed
// compiler -- `memory access out of bounds` inside `__rt_rc_alloc`. That is not
// this bug: `assign_self_borrow_use` in that file corrupts the free list (#2786,
// still open), the damage surfaces on a later allocation, and a function
// appended after it merely supplies one. A case that fails both ways
// discriminates nothing, and that file's own header says so about the #2786
// shape. Read from here: a new RC value case goes in its own file until it is
// shown to answer differently on the two compilers, because a shared file can
// hand it a heap that has already been damaged.
enum Node {
  Leaf(Int);
  Pair(Node, Node)
}

struct Holder {
  node: Node
}

fn total(n: Node) -> Int {
  match n {
    Pair(a, b) => total(a) + total(b),
    Leaf(v) => v
  }
}

fn assign_borrow_bound_binder_proj(hs: Array[Holder]) -> Int {
  let mut x = Pair(Leaf(1), Leaf(2))
  x = {
    let h = Array::get(hs, 0)
    h.node
  }
  let r = total(x)
  let filler = Pair(Leaf(7), Leaf(8))
  r * 100 + total(Array::get(hs, 0).node) * 10 + total(filler) * 0
}

test "2796 a wrapped projection rooted at a borrow-bound binder retains" {
  let hs = [Holder::{ node: Pair(Leaf(3), Leaf(4)) }]
  inspect(assign_borrow_bound_binder_proj(hs), content = "770")
}
